{"id": "2026-08-25-news-us-drops-syria-from-terror-sponsor-list", "date": "2026-08-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "US drops Syria from terror-sponsor list", "summary": "Washington rescinded Syria's 47-year state-sponsor-of-terrorism designation and delisted HTS.", "url": "https://www.state.gov/releases/office-of-the-spokesperson/2026/08/rescission-of-syrias-designation-as-a-state-sponsor-of-terrorism/", "source_domain": "state.gov", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "The United States removed Syria from its list of state sponsors of terrorism on Monday 24 August, ending a designation that had stood for 47 years, and separately delisted the group now governing the country. Secretary of State Marco Rubio said he had authorised the \"formal rescission\" of Syria's state-sponsor-of-terrorism (SST) label — a status, held since 1979, that all but barred US investment and dealings with Damascus — after the mandatory 45-day period for notifying Congress ran out. He also removed Hay'at Tahrir al-Sham from the \"Specially Designated Global Terrorist\" list. Rubio cast the moves as recognition of \"positive actions\" by al-Sharaa's government to \"distance Syria from acts of international terrorism,\" including joining the US-led anti-ISIS coalition; that is the administration's framing of a leadership whose own roots are in jihadist insurgency, and the practical aim, as Le Temps notes, is to open the country to investment. The steps follow a June 2025 executive order that had already begun dismantling the Syria sanctions program.", "why": "lifting the terror labels is the legal gate that lets banks, insurers and investors — European ones included — re-engage with Syria, so it matters far beyond Washington for how fast the post-Assad economy can reopen.", "thread_id": "2026-08-25-news-us-drops-syria-from-terror-sponsor-list", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-25", "event_date": "2026-08-24", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["United States", "Syria", "Hayat Tahrir al-Sham", "Ahmed al-Sharaa", "Marco Rubio"]}
{"id": "2026-08-25-news-canada-readies-retaliation-as-us-tariffs-bite", "date": "2026-08-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Canada readies retaliation as US tariffs bite", "summary": "Canada will impose counter-tariffs on 8 September after US 50% duties took effect and talks collapsed.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/canada-set-to-announce-retaliatory-tariffs-on-us-goods-after-talks-fail/a-78491819", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["economy", "geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Canada is due to unveil retaliatory tariffs on Tuesday 25 August after US duties of 50% took effect and trade talks collapsed, deepening a rupture between the two neighbours. The new fact since the tariffs landed on 22 August: Ottawa says its counter-measures will take effect on 8 September, and Prime Minister Mark Carney has publicly refused what he calls a \"bad deal,\" rejecting US demands that he \"fall in line\" — President Trump's phrase. The US levy hits roughly $20 billion of Canadian goods; Trump has separately threatened 50% tariffs on Canadian autos and steel from 2027. Talks broke down only days after Trump had said the two sides were close to an agreement.", "why": "the US–Canada relationship is one of the world's largest trade partnerships, and a tit-for-tat escalation between two treaty allies signals how far the administration's tariff strategy now reaches — a warning sign for other trade-exposed economies, Switzerland among them.", "thread_id": "2026-08-22-weekend-us-imposes-50-tariffs-on-canadian-goods", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-22", "event_date": "2026-08-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Canada", "United States", "Mark Carney", "Donald Trump"]}
{"id": "2026-08-25-news-third-drone-found-at-leipzig-airport", "date": "2026-08-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Third drone found at Leipzig airport", "summary": "Investigators found a third drone and suspected explosives at Leipzig/Halle; Russian intelligence suspected.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-third-drone-found-in-leipzig-airport-probe/live-78491814", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["security", "geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A third drone and suspected explosives were found near Leipzig/Halle Airport, German media reported on Tuesday 25 August, widening an investigation that security sources link to Russian intelligence. The find follows an explosives-laden drone discovered earlier this month beside a Ukrainian cargo aircraft used to move military supplies through the eastern German hub — the incident that opened the probe. German investigators are treating the case as possible sabotage; security sources cited by German outlets suspect Russian intelligence involvement, which Moscow denies.", "why": "the airport is a logistics node for Western aid to Ukraine, and repeated drone incursions on NATO soil sharpen European fears that the war's sabotage front is reaching inside the alliance.", "thread_id": "2026-08-06-news-explosive-drone-found-at-leipzig-airport", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-06", "event_date": "2026-08-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Leipzig/Halle Airport", "Germany", "Russia", "Ukraine"]}
{"id": "2026-08-25-news-tornado-devastates-southern-french-village", "date": "2026-08-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Tornado devastates southern French village", "summary": "A tornado hit Pomas in the Aude, injuring around 40 and damaging some 300 homes.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/tornado-in-france-damages-homes-injures-dozens/a-78491206", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A tornado tore through the southern French village of Pomas on Monday 24 August, injuring around 40 people and damaging roughly 300 homes. Pomas, a community of about 1,000 in the Aude foothills of the Pyrenees, was hit hardest; the storm uprooted trees and ripped roofs from buildings. Fifteen of the injured were taken to hospital, among them a pregnant woman whose house collapsed while she was inside, and more than 120 firefighters and emergency staff were deployed, with shelters set up for those left homeless. France's national weather service, Météo-France, said the tornado packed winds of up to 117 km/h.", "why": "destructive tornadoes are rare in France, and a direct strike on a village underscores how localized extreme-weather events can level a small community in minutes.", "thread_id": "2026-08-25-news-tornado-devastates-southern-french-village", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-25", "event_date": "2026-08-24", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Pomas", "France", "Meteo-France"]}
{"id": "2026-08-25-news-gang-massacre-at-haiti-church-shelter", "date": "2026-08-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Gang massacre at Haiti church shelter", "summary": "Gunmen killed at least 40 displaced people at a church camp above Port-au-Prince.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/haiti-gang-members-kill-dozens-near-port-au-prince/a-78491117", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world", "security"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Gang members killed at least 40 people, some execution-style, in an overnight attack on a displaced-persons shelter near Haiti's capital, the local mayor and the UN said on Monday 24 August. The gunmen raided a camp housing displaced families inside a church in Kenscoff, a town in the hills above Port-au-Prince that has faced months of gang violence, according to mayor Massillon Jean, who described \"a night of terror.\" Many of the victims had already fled earlier violence; several people were abducted and dozens wounded, and searches for the missing continued. Residents have called for the local police chief to resign over allegations that officers failed to protect those sheltering in the church.", "why": "it is one of the deadliest single attacks in Haiti's long gang crisis, and the failure to shield a displaced-persons site points to how far the state's control has eroded around the capital.", "thread_id": "2026-08-25-news-gang-massacre-at-haiti-church-shelter", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-25", "event_date": "2026-08-23", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Haiti", "Kenscoff", "Port-au-Prince"]}
{"id": "2026-08-25-news-us-to-revoke-asylum-seeker-visas", "date": "2026-08-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "US to revoke asylum-seeker visas", "summary": "The State Department will revoke tourist and business visas of foreigners who sought asylum, up to 200,000 per AP.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/us-trump-administration-plans-to-revoke-up-to-200-000-visas-from-asylum-seekers/a-78491300", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The US State Department said on Monday 24 August it will revoke the tourist and business visas of foreigners who applied for asylum after entering on those visas — a step the Associated Press estimates could affect up to 200,000 people. The department's statement did not itself give a figure; the AP's up-to-200,000 estimate, if borne out, would make this the largest mass visa revocation in US history. The measure targets people who entered on non-immigrant (visitor or business) visas and then sought asylum, which the administration casts as visa misuse.", "why": "it is a further tightening of legal-immigration channels rather than border enforcement, and the headline number is an outside estimate, not an official count — worth watching for how many revocations actually issue.", "thread_id": "2026-08-25-news-us-to-revoke-asylum-seeker-visas", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-25", "event_date": "2026-08-24", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["United States", "State Department"]}
{"id": "2026-08-25-news-valais-village-braces-for-glacier-collapse", "date": "2026-08-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Valais village braces for glacier collapse", "summary": "Randa sealed a hazard zone as the Weisshorn Ost hanging glacier could break off within days.", "url": "https://www.nzz.ch/panorama/in-der-walliser-gemeinde-randa-droht-ein-gletscherabbruch-am-weisshorn-ld.10020894", "source_domain": "nzz.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The Valais village of Randa sealed off a danger zone on Tuesday 25 August after warning that a hanging glacier above the village could break away within days. The commune said monitoring of the Weisshorn Ost hanging glacier (a mass of ice clinging to a steep slope, prone to sudden collapse) had detected the ice moving faster, and it has stepped up observation and defined a no-go hazard zone that must not be entered until further notice. According to the commune's map, only a few individual buildings fall inside the zone; most of the village lies just outside but very close to it. Randa knows the risk: in spring 1991 one of the largest rockfalls in 20th-century Europe — some 30 million cubic metres — crashed toward the valley here, damming the Mattervispa river and flooding parts of the village, and the disaster spurred Switzerland to develop early-warning technology for rockfalls. The warning also comes months after the glacier collapse that buried the village of Blatten.", "why": "it is a direct, immediate hazard for residents of the Mattertal (the valley linking Visp to Zermatt), and another instance of the accelerating Alpine instability that Swiss mountain communities are now managing in real time.", "thread_id": "2026-08-25-news-valais-village-braces-for-glacier-collapse", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-25", "event_date": "2026-08-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Randa", "Valais", "Weisshorn", "Mattertal"]}
{"id": "2026-08-25-news-bernese-seeland-plans-major-irrigation", "date": "2026-08-25", "stream": "news", "headline": "Bernese Seeland plans major irrigation", "summary": "Farmers near Ins plan one of Switzerland's largest irrigation systems as drought bites.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/berner-flurgenossenschaft-wegen-duerre-bewaesserungsprojekt-im-berner-seeland-geplant", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Farmers in the Bernese Seeland are planning one of Switzerland's largest agricultural irrigation systems as drought bites, SRF reported on Tuesday 25 August. The \"generational\" project near Ins, in canton Bern, would lay some 90 kilometres of underground pipes fed by electric pumps to bring water to about 1,700 hectares of farmland — a scheme running to millions of francs and, per SRF, among the biggest of its kind in the country. It responds to a summer of severe drought; the federal authorities cautioned this week that recent rain has not offset the deficit, and Swiss rivers and lakes remain unusually low.", "why": "the Seeland is one of Switzerland's most important vegetable-growing regions, and building permanent irrigation on this scale signals that farmers are treating recurring drought as a structural condition to engineer around, not a one-off bad year.", "thread_id": "2026-08-25-news-bernese-seeland-plans-major-irrigation", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-25", "event_date": "2026-08-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Seeland", "Ins", "Bern"]}
